Unreleased language branch: sort(values) orders a numeric or Bool array in place and returns that same array; sorted(values) returns an independent sorted array. Both use the same deterministic ordering, including a defined order for NaNs and signed zeros. See the collection-functions reference for ordering, task-reader restrictions and cancellation behavior.

